Z||000000||87fiero_gt||06-25-99||05:47 PM||||I have multiple problems. I have to jiggle the key to get the ignition switch out of lock. Now the car starts but only runs for a second or two. It will do this twice and then only crank and won't fire. I am going to replace the dist. cap and rotor, they didn't look too good and probably the ignition module. Any help is appreciated.
Z||000001||theogre||06-25-99||10:32 PM||||check all the battery wires very carefully. the small wire from B+ (battery +) can cause all sort of things if it's damaged. Other wise your current plan for testing is good, but make sure you unplug the tach filter first. The T.F. can short out, and when it does it shorts the coil to ground and keeps the dist module from firing the thing.<p>as for the lock problem, I guess you have an auto tranny? Try pushing forward on the shifter while turning the key. If it now turns easily, you need to adjust the interlock cable. If that doesn't help you may have a worn out lock, or lock linkage, and that has to be replaced.<p>If you don't have the tools to remove the steering wheel and "lock plate" it might be cheaper and/or easier to just get a good used steering column. The tools are around 30-40$us, the lock is another X number of dolars, and the project takes a fair amount of time. ((The lock plate is a pain to get off even with the tool)) Most of the time you can find a steering column for less than 100$. GM used those columns in a bunch of small cars. there are 5 bolts/nuts that connect the column and a few electrical plugs. ((you MUST remove the bolt in the universal joint. the shaft is notched and will not come out untill the bolt is gone.))
Z||000002||four50four||07-10-99||04:03 PM||||well about your key lockage problem, my prelude used to do that just had to jiggle the steering wheel, same with my dads truck and with my moms 97 taurus wagon i once accidenlty turned the wheel till it locked and the key wouldn't move. had to reef on the steering wheel as hard as i could till it came loose, and this vehicle has less then 30000 miles on it so... 
